  "id": "Compound::DB00786 - Gene::4326",
  "verbalization": "Marimastat is likely to interact with Mmp17 through a shared pathway involving matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs). The evidence suggests that Marimastat binds to Mmp23b, Mmp27, and Mmp26, all of which are part of the MMP family and are participated by Mmp17. This indicates that Marimastat may influence Mmp17 through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating MMP activity. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, implying that Marimastat's interaction with these MMPs may have a broad impact on Mmp17. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Marimastat to regulate MMP activity, which in turn could affect Mmp17. The evidence supports a mechanism where Marimastat's binding to MMPs leads to a downstream effect on Mmp17, though the exact nature of this effect remains to be determined.",
